             "Water contains chlorine or chloramine — kills bacteria",
             "Jar too narrow — CO₂ cannot expand the culture"],
            ["Place jar in a warm spot (24–26 °C) — top of the fridge, inside an oven with just the light on",
             "Switch to unbleached bread flour or add 20% rye",
             "Use filtered water or leave tap water uncovered overnight to off-gas chlorine",
             "Use a wider, straight-sided jar — a tall narrow jar suppresses rise visually",
             "If < 14 days old: be patient and keep feeding daily"]),
        new("📉", "Rises then collapses too fast", "Moderate", "warn",
            ["Kitchen is very warm (26 °C+) — fermentation races to peak and beyond",
             "Ratio too low (1:1:1 in warm conditions) — not enough food for the activity level",
             "Starter was already overdue a feed before you fed it"],
            ["Move to a cooler spot or feed at a higher ratio (1:5:5)",
             "Use cold water to slow the feed",
             "Feed on a fixed schedule rather than waiting for collapse"]),
        new("🧪", "Too sour — unpleasant sharp or acetone smell", "Cosmetic", "low",
            ["Acetic acid dominant — starter is cold, infrequently fed, or very stiff",
             "Starter left too long between feeds",
             "Using a very stiff culture (< 65% hydration)"],
            ["Feed more frequently or increase the ratio to 1:5:5",
             "Move to a warmer location — warmth favours lactic (milder) over acetic (sharper) acid",
             "Increase hydration slightly — a wetter culture favours lactic bacteria"]),
        new("😶", "Not sour enough / bland flavour", "Cosmetic", "low",
            ["Feeding too frequently — acids are diluted before they build",
             "Kitchen too warm — fast fermentation gives yeast priority over acid producers",
             "Always using at peak — some acidity develops after peak"],
            ["Reduce feeding frequency or use at just-past-peak rather than at peak",
             "Try a cooler fermentation temperature",
             "Add 10–20% rye to the feed flour — rye produces a more flavourful culture"]),
        new("💧", "Grey or brown liquid on top (hooch)", "Minor", "ok",
